    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (72.39) anchoring the lineup, both benefiting from favorable matchups against pitchers with xERAs above 4.50. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is our premier play, as he draws a soft matchup against Pecko; his dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and favorable #3 spot in the order make him an essential anchor for our offensive production. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** (71.12) continues to be an automatic start despite a mid-tier matchup, as his efficiency rating remains elevated by superior underlying metrics that transcend daily park or pitcher-specific noise.\n\nThe strategy today focuses on maximizing volume against weaker arms while navigating several high-stress matchups. While **Nasim Nunez** (53.45) is currently in the lineup, we are monitoring his low order position, which creates a slight drag on his overall efficiency. The most difficult decision rested with **Miguel Vargas** (39.33), who just missed the cut for the active roster. While he boasts a strong xwOBA of .389, the combination of facing a high-caliber arm in deGrom and the specific scarcity of our category needs\u2014particularly our weighting toward speed\u2014pushed him just below our 40.0 floor. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Jackson Merrill** (49.36) and **Sam Antonacci** (43.60); both face the significant hurdle of Paul Skenes and deGrom, respectively. Their scores reflect the reality that elite pitching arms, specifically those with high strikeout potential, cap the ceiling for even our most talented hitters. We will be closely watching for any weather updates in these high-leverage games, as any delay could jeopardize our pursuit of category efficiency.",
